You have epiblepharon in one or both eyes. Epiblepharon is a common eyelid condition, especially in children, in which an extra fold of skin pushes the eyelashes inward toward the surface of the eye.\
\
Because the eyelashes are directed toward the cornea, they can rub against the front of the eye when blinking. This may cause tearing, irritation, redness, light sensitivity, or the feeling that something is in the eye. In some children it causes little discomfort, while in others it can irritate the corneal surface.\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

